  "documentation": {
	"summary": "The historical four-corner pyramid court and separate higher Durer platform restored inside the museum.",
	"layout": "13x23 hall. Opening 5x5 court at x3..7,z3..7, one metre above the museum floor: four corner pyramids, central spire, four small cubes. The puzzle stands beside the court at (9,3). A raised connection leads to the separate 5x5 Durer platform at x3..7,z14..18, two metres above the floor. Open circulation runs around both stages. Exit at (6,21) has a landing row behind it; the museum fills its grid teleporter void.",
	"key_elements": ["Pale blue corner pyramids, 2.4 m tall, at (3,3),(7,3),(3,7),(7,7); pink pyramidlong with matching 0.8 m pedestal at (5,5)", "Ochre cubes, 0.8 m sides, at (5,4),(4,5),(6,5),(5,6); lower faces meet the court", "wp:90 at (2,5) reaches the first deck; wp:0 at (5,13) reaches the second", "Durer tableau at (5,15), rotation 180, scale 0.5", "Paired frames at (2,11),(9,11); supporting solids remain", "Platforms exist independently of puzzle completion"],
	"restoration": {
	  "source_commit": "4beaa29b89ea1fe297fab7d747a6c44624d01bb1",
	  "source_path": "commons/maps/Primitives_Melencolia/map_data.json",
	  "date": "2026-09-08",
	  "adaptation": "Court translated +2,+8 cells; historic1m/2m elevations and half-scale cubes/tableau retained. Durer deck enlarged to support the current tableau footprint; surrounding museum floor and entry/exit retained. Removed stale differently-sized museum-layer snapshot; live museum derives from structure. Two extra rear circulation rows added after actual-museum physics exposed an automatic sculpture narrowing the original return route.",
	  "current_revision": {
		"date": "2026-09-16",
		"comparison_commit": "86d423341",
		"change": "Removed the preceding booth so the geometric court is the opening encounter. Restored the second historical side frame. Moved the puzzle beside the court after checking the actual museum view. All pre-existing artifact types retained.",
		"references": ["https://pdimagearchive.org/images/4577a16c-d0e9-43d6-96fc-f125c47c6afe/", "https://publicdomainreview.org/collection/solid-objects/"],
		"image_refinement": "User supplied the selected manuscript image: slender blue corner pyramids, pink central spire on a matching cubical base, ochre cubes between the corners. Colours and proportions now follow that image while preserving the restored walkable layout. Dimensions are a museum adaptation, not measurements from the drawing."
	  }
